Z||000000||loafer87gt||10-31-2001||08:06 PM||||Emergency here. Halloween party starts in three hours and I haven't thought of a costume yet. I thought I might as well just make a toga out of a bedsheet but I can't figure out how the heck you fold it or what to do. I did a search on google and it came up with a couple sites that had directions but I wasn't able to make any sense of them. There must be some of ex phrat boys and girls on the forum here that could give me an idiots guide to making a toga, right? TIA||||reg||6
Z||000001||yo_sweets_babe||10-31-2001||08:09 PM||||if i knew how to, i'd tell u<P>all i can say is, GOOD LUCK AND HAVE FUN||||reg||6
Z||000002||Hank is Here||10-31-2001||08:45 PM||||just try a sheet over your shoulder and try safety pinning it togther on the other side<P>Also one other good costume I saw was Osama bin Laden.  Towel on your head, bathrobe, beard, and shirt with a target on it.  Not my idea but very funny--and also very ballzie||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||10-31-2001||08:49 PM||||GOT IT (I think... haven't read it yet)!!!<P>Am I too late???<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ronturner.org/howtomakeatoga.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ronturner.org/howtomakeatoga.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||10-31-2001||08:53 PM||||You're fast, Cheeve, but this one's better. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">Wrap it around your waist a time or two if long enough. Pin it to itself. Throw the remainder over your shoulder, bring that part around from the back to the waist again. You'll have to play with it(no pun intended) to get it to look right. Wear shorts under it.(very important, a sheet isn't very long. Or go here, use the scroll arrows in the middle left of the page. <A HREF="http://www.gotpip.com/toga.cfm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gotpip.com/toga.cfm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever3000||10-31-2001||09:06 PM||||Dewd, there's actually a FORUM for this!!!<BR>Let's go! (sorry Cliff, just temporary)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.party411.com/forum/messages/947.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.party411.com/forum/messages/947.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever3000||10-31-2001||09:09 PM||||I'll edit this post with any others I find.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.artemissoftware.com/toga/toga_tips.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.artemissoftware.com/toga/toga_tips.html</A> <P><BR>Some more pictures, might be helpful... <A HREF="http://www.funfolly.com/h/ca05a.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.funfolly.com/h/ca05a.htm</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||JSocha||10-31-2001||10:15 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> Wrap corner "A" around to corner "B".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">  Now take free corner "C" insert it into the now formed "D" formerly created by "A-B" making sure plenty of edge "E" is remaining.  Now take edge "E", wrap around to "A" over shoulder "F".<P>Here's where it gets really tricky.<P>If you have any sheet left, your a small dude.  If you find yourself comprimized in certain areas, you be too big for any sheet for toga and would be better going as Casper, A very FRIENDLY GHOST!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Of course, that will require the optional bed sheet with punch outs "C" and "E" and optional punch outs "A" and "B".<P>I just wish I could have found the Calvin and Hobbs version of making a Toga out of moms best sheets.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000008||Cheever3000||11-01-2001||12:48 AM||||Just punch a hole in the middle for your head, and wear it like a poncho.  Add something for a belt, like a piece of rope.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||loafer87gt||11-01-2001||02:37 PM||||Well, the toga thing didn't pan out. We ended up painting ourselves blue and made up a bunch of garb out of beer boxes and went as the beer avengers. It all worked out good tho, I ended up taking home a cute girl dressed up as a smurf  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> cha ching!||||reg||1
